## SS-C1. Render spec → HTML → PDF (two steps, one block)

Chrome is already installed at `/Applications/Google Chrome.app`. Node is at `/opt/homebrew/bin/node`. No npm install, no new dependency.

```bash
# Step 1: spec.json → HTML via renderer (validates spec shape and applies locked visual template)
node "$RENDERER" "$SPEC" "$HTML" 2>&1
RENDER_RC=$?
if [ $RENDER_RC -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "renderer failed rc=$RENDER_RC — log Type=Error Reason=spec_render_failed"; exit 1
fi
test -f "$HTML" || { echo "renderer produced no HTML — log Type=Error Reason=no_html_output"; exit 1; }

# Step 2: HTML → PDF via headless Chrome
"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome" \
  --headless \
  --disable-gpu \
  --no-pdf-header-footer \
  --no-margins \
  --virtual-time-budget=3000 \
  --print-to-pdf="$PDF" \
  "file://$HTML" 2>&1
```

🚨 **Verify PDF output:**
```bash
test -f "$PDF" || { echo "PDF render failed — log Type=Error Reason=pdf_render_failed"; exit 1; }
SIZE=$(stat -f%z "$PDF")
test "$SIZE" -gt 20000 || { echo "PDF suspiciously small ($SIZE bytes) — log Type=Error Reason=pdf_too_small"; exit 1; }
# Heuristic page count — renderer produces exactly 10 slides; anything else is a red flag
PAGES=$(python3 -c "import re; print(len(re.findall(rb'/Type\s*/Page[^s]', open('$PDF','rb').read())))")
echo "PDF OK: $SIZE bytes, $PAGES pages"
```

Capture `$SIZE` and `$PAGES` for SS-C7 logging. If PAGES > 10, log `Type=Warning` and continue (still posts).

