## SS-C3. Arm upload, click Choose file label

🚨 **Arm BEFORE click.** The upload endpoint intercepts the next `Page.fileChooserOpened`. Clicking first pops the OS dialog and blocks.

```bash
# Arm (blocks until chooser opens + file delivered, or timeout)
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/upload -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d "{\"filePath\":\"${PDF}\",\"timeoutMs\":60000}" > /tmp/upload-result.json &
UPLOAD_PID=$!
sleep 1

# Click the label (fires chooser that the arm intercepts)
exec curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3847/api/browser/{{browser_profile}}/evaluate -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d @- <<'ENDJSON'
{"fn":"async () => { var shadow = document.querySelector('#interop-outlet').shadowRoot; var label = Array.from(shadow.querySelectorAll('label')).find(function(l) { return (l.innerText||'').trim() === 'Choose file'; }); if (!label) return { success: false, reason: 'no_choose_file_label' }; label.click(); return { success: true }; }"}
ENDJSON

wait $UPLOAD_PID
grep -q '"ok":true' /tmp/upload-result.json || { echo "upload failed:"; cat /tmp/upload-result.json; exit 1; }
```

LinkedIn processes the PDF server-side (~3-6s).

