## SS-C7. Log + limits update

🚨 Agent substitutes every `<<TOKEN>>` at compose time (shell sees only final strings). Tokens: `<<DATE>>` (`date +%Y-%m-%d`), `<<TIME>>` (`date +%H:%M`), `<<TITLE>>` (from .md), `<<POST_URL>>` (SS-C6), `<<PDF_PATH>>`/`<<PDF_SIZE>>`/`<<PDF_PAGES>>` (SS-C1), `<<DOC_PATH>>` ($DOC), `<<COMMENT_CHARS>>` (SS-C5).

### Block 1 — memory log

```bash
cat >> {{opentwins_home}}agent-linkedin/memory/<<DATE>>.md <<'EOF'
## <<DATE>> <<TIME>> - Carousel Published
- Title: <<TITLE>>
- URL: <<POST_URL>>
- PDF: <<PDF_PATH>> (<<PDF_SIZE>> bytes, <<PDF_PAGES>> pages)
- Source doc: <<DOC_PATH>>
- Commentary chars: <<COMMENT_CHARS>>
EOF
```

### Block 2 — increment `weekly.carousels.current`

🚨 `.slice(-4)` (robust across Node versions' `process.argv` layouts).

```bash
node -e '
  const fs = require("fs");
  const [title, url, date, time] = process.argv.slice(-4);
  const path = "{{opentwins_home}}agent-linkedin/limits.json";
  const j = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path, "utf8"));
  j.weekly = j.weekly || {};
  if (!j.weekly.carousels) {
    j.weekly.carousels = { limit: 2, current: 0, last_reset: date, week_start: "monday", history: [] };
  }
  j.weekly.carousels.current = (j.weekly.carousels.current || 0) + 1;
  j.weekly.carousels.history = j.weekly.carousels.history || [];
  j.weekly.carousels.history.unshift({ date, time, title, url });
  fs.writeFileSync(path, JSON.stringify(j, null, 2));
  console.log("carousels.current =", j.weekly.carousels.current);
' '<<TITLE>>' '<<POST_URL>>' '<<DATE>>' '<<TIME>>'
```

🚨 Arg order fixed: TITLE, POST_URL, DATE, TIME.

### Block 3 — mark `linkedin-carousel.md` as published

```bash
node -e '
  const fs = require("fs");
  const path = process.argv.slice(-1)[0];
  const body = fs.readFileSync(path, "utf8");
  const next = body.replace(/^status: pending$/m, "status: published");
  if (next === body) { console.error("no status: pending line found in " + path); process.exit(1); }
  fs.writeFileSync(path, next);
  console.log("marked published");
' '<<DOC_PATH>>'
```

### Verify all three landed

```bash
# Memory log appended (grep for today's Title line)
grep -c "Carousel Published" {{opentwins_home}}agent-linkedin/memory/<<DATE>>.md

# limits.json increment
node -e '
  const j = JSON.parse(require("fs").readFileSync("{{opentwins_home}}agent-linkedin/limits.json","utf8"));
  console.log("carousels:", j.weekly.carousels.current, "/", j.weekly.carousels.limit);
'

# Status flipped in doc
grep "^status:" '<<DOC_PATH>>'
```

If any verify fails: re-run the failed block (log + status flip are idempotent; JSON increment is NOT — only rerun if `current` didn't advance).

